    "note": "O'Rourke & Korenaga 2015 (PDF p. 2, txt 147–149): «Some authors favor a relatively thick lithosphere, usually 200–400 km (e.g., Turcotte, 1993; Solomatov and Moresi, 1996), but data permit values as high as 600 km (Orth and Solomatov, 2011). Thinner (100 km) lithosphere allows a larger magnitude of melt generation to explain recent resurfacing». No single value is printed; 300 km is **our** midpoint of the «usually 200–400 km» band — a choice, not a reading. Foley eq. (3) needs one δ, so a value must be declared; the band (100–600 km) is the sensitivity to report. Mars's 330 km (Morschhauser+ 2011, model output) is a different body and is not transferred.\n"
